* @title Storage regeneration and function-local variables
* @attribution Griswold 1971, Chapter 11
* @match substring
* @mask-line ^FREE SPACE BEFORE:  :: COLLECT() returns the free space the IMPLEMENTATION has left, so its value belongs to SPITBOL's allocator and not to this program. MEASURED (hq_V 2026-09-08, sbl -bf, three runs each): a bare COLLECT() reads 129577 every time, and 129570 after the program allocates one 40-character string -- deterministic, and moving unit for unit with SPITBOL's own string space. Ours reports our heap and can never equal it. The remaining three lines are graded normally; this fixture's author had already ruled this line ungradable by leaving it out of @expect above, and CEO-409 restores that judgement.
* @expect >>>
* LOCALS ARE NULL: 
* GLOBALS RESTORED: STAY STAY
* <<<
         OUTPUT = 'FREE SPACE BEFORE: ' COLLECT()
         DEFINE('RESET(X,Y,Z)')               :(START)
RESET    OUTPUT = 'LOCALS ARE NULL: ' IDENT(X) IDENT(Y)
         :(RETURN)
START    X = 'STAY'; Y = 'STAY'
         RESET()
         OUTPUT = 'GLOBALS RESTORED: ' X ' ' Y
END
